 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad 17 or newer to be in the path.
 To install from a different drive than DF0: select installation mode Expert.

 The installed game requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 1 MB OtherMem (Kickstart ROM
 and Enhanced framerate), plus memory for preload. An A500 without Fast memory
 and an A1200 without Fast memory do not have enough.
 It can be quit by pressing F10 (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from a A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on aminet.
 If the image is of wrong version or altered in any way WHDLoad will quit with
 an appropriate message.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on aminet.


 Features:
 ---------
 - Full load from HD
 - 2 versions supported
 - Protection removed (disk check)
 - Access fault fixed
 - Crash when starting race fixed
 - Wrong blit fixed
 - CPU dependent delay fixed
 - Sound stop delay fixed (stalls and freezes on a 68040/060 with caches)
 - Timing fixed
 - Manual included 
 - lots of nice icons (one created by me, all others by Irek)
 - Source code included as usual
 - Quit option that works on 68000 machines (default key is 'F10')
 - Enhanced framerate (CUSTOM2=1) for the PAL SPS 0481 version

 Enhanced framerate keeps the game speed constant whatever the rendering
 speed and renders faster. On a 68020 or faster with Fast memory the player's
 car moves more smoothly. On a 68030 or faster with Fast memory the picture
 is drawn in Fast memory. It uses Fast memory and the safe CPU caches when
 available. The installed icon enables it (CUSTOM2=1); set CUSTOM2=0 to run
 the game as before.
 Irek's version keeps its original behaviour.

 Finally this patch is finished, started it back in 2013, disabled the
 protection and then tried to find the reason for the crash that happened
 when starting a race. The game uses overlay hunks and is programmed in C
 which didn't make things any easier at all. It looked like an interrupt bug
 but actually it wasn't, real problem was using a register without properly
 initialising it which in turn trashed the screen pointer. There also was a
 similar problem when leaving the race track, this one caused a completely
 wrong and buggy blitter operation and was also caused by using a register
 without initialising it. Fixing these two bugs took me a long time but finally
 the game works without problems!

 As the game was made for the A500 the coder didn't wait for the raster beam
 which means the game runs much too fast on anything else than a plain 68000
 machine. I have fixed the timing of course.

 Enjoy the game from HD.
 Sting, 01-Aug-2016


